    {
      "id": "b84c63dd0926",
      "name": "Daily Chief morning health summary",
      "prompt": "Run the Railway Chief health check and send DJ a concise daily Chief/Railway health update in plain English.\n\nRun exactly:\nCHIEF_HEALTH_ALWAYS_REPORT=1 /opt/data/scripts/chief_health_check.sh\n\nReport in a compact, human-readable format. Include:\n- One-line verdict using these meanings:\n  - \"All clear\" only when checks are OK.\n  - \"Hermes follow-up logged\" when the output says DJ action is none / issues are not DJ-actionable.\n  - \"DJ action needed\" only when the output explicitly says DJ action is required or the gateway/resources are unhealthy.\n- A \"Useful context\" section with:\n  - Memory usage: amount used / total / percent\n  - Railway volume usage: amount used / total / percent\n  - Gateway status: running or not\n  - Any operational issue details if present\n- Last backup status if visible in /opt/data/health/last_status.txt or the health output.\n- DJ action line.\n\nRules:\n- Do not say \"attention needed\" if the recommended DJ action is none.\n- Do not dump raw logs unless there is a real failure.\n- Keep it friendly and brief: roughly 5-8 short lines.",
